
(note BZ-AriaModelProvenance-01-neg)
(time 240)

; Negative control for BZ-AriaModelProvenance-01.
;
; Same inference, same model, but the model has now been archived for
; a compliance-impacting cause (a discovered vulnerability that calls
; prior outputs into question).
;
; The default LLM answer to "is this older inference still admissible?"
; is yes ("the inference was valid when made"). The formalism does not
; agree. Admissibility is a function of the model's CURRENT compliance
; status, not its status at inference time.
;
; Note: this is the right policy for vulnerability-driven archival.
; Routine performance-driven rotation is a different case and would
; not assert modelArchivedForCause.
;
; Expected verdict: the conjecture must NOT be provable.

(instance aria01Gemma3v13 AriaModel)
(instance inference17 AriaInference)

(inferenceFromModel inference17 aria01Gemma3v13)

; DIFFERENCE FROM POSITIVE CASE: model is now archived for cause
(modelArchivedForCause aria01Gemma3v13)

(query (admissibleForCompliance inference17))

(answer no)
